          "hypothesis_as_declared_by_model": "An inward-scanning Hoare partition can reduce writes and keep partition reads sequential from both ends, while a small insertion-sort cutoff improves locality on tiny ranges. Processing the larger partition iteratively also bounds recursion depth without changing the generated data or sorted output.",
