          "hypothesis_as_declared_by_model": "The bucket-count and scatter passes have loop-carried dependencies because multiple elements may target the same bucket, so they cannot safely be marked SIMD. For sufficiently large inputs, per-thread histograms and cursors over disjoint input chunks can remove cross-thread conflicts while preserving exact bucket ranges; this may reduce serial preprocessing time before the existing parallel bucket sorts.",
