        "hypothesis_as_declared_by_model": "A workload-aware combination should outperform the baseline across obstacle densities: factorial-based first-hit counting avoids scanning the grid when obstacles are very sparse, while a tiled OpenMP wavefront handles large dense grids; smaller grids and non-OpenMP builds retain a compact rolling-row DP.",
        "transformations_as_declared_by_model": {
